      "math_academy_id": "e-4705",
      "problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14118900/assets/b7bd0927ad34eb75ec2d6e7d03509b983e8a90e8846c42b2da6e6898cb50afa3.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$",
